# Always surface setup — never omit, never dump it on Hugo

Hugo must never discover missing setup after the fact. If a change depends on anything outside the code, **the agent does it**. Tell him in Swedish only if something still blocks *him*.

## Agent does this (do not ask Hugo)

1. **NUMA SQL / migrations** — apply via Supabase MCP to `hadrtlancgopyyshwhyd`, schema `numa`. File in `supabase/migrations/`. Local `supabase db push` is only if he tests locally and MCP already applied remote.
2. **Vercel** — preview deploy happens on push. Env vars, domains, canonical URL: Vercel MCP. Redeploy if env changed.
3. **Git** — always commit + push the feature branch. Ask **Preview eller produktion?** before merging to `main`. Merge to production only when he says produktion.

## Tell Hugo only when it actually blocks him

- A secret only he has (e.g. a new `OPENAI_API_KEY` he has not created).
- MCP/SQL/Vercel failed and needs a dashboard click he must do.
- Auth redirect / billing / something no API can do.

Put a short **“Du behöver göra detta”** block **only** in those cases. Prefer checklist. Blocking = say it with the preview-vs-produktion question, not after he tries and fails.

If nothing blocks him, do **not** invent a “kör denna SQL” checklist.
